    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable schedule today, headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** is our most efficient play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against L\u00f3pez, R, where his ability to exploit a slow-delivering pitcher significantly boosts his steal probability. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives in his matchup against Lorenzen; despite hitting lower in the order, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and dynamic platoon advantages pushes his efficiency well into the elite tier. Both **Nasim Nunez** (68.97) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.85) also serve as critical engines for our squad, with **Nasim Nunez** providing unique speed potential from the bottom of the order and **Heliot Ramos** maintaining a strong profile despite the minor defensive risk posed by the opposing catcher.\n\nStrategic volatility is centered around the Lorenzen start, which presents both high-ceiling opportunities and weather-related concerns. **Curtis Mead** (62.15), **Nasim Nunez**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** are all tied to this matchup, and while the park and SP skill factors are optimal, we are monitoring a 33% rain risk that could threaten the entire stack. On the bench, **Gunnar Henderson** (57.32) was the final exclusion; while his raw talent is undeniable, he is currently suppressed by a negative platoon adjustment against Rivera, Ed, and lower projected efficiency compared to our primary starters. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Kyle Tucker** (56.32) and **Andy Pages** (50.50), as they face the difficult Wheeler. While their base projections remain steady, the matchup against such an elite arm effectively caps their scoring potential for the day.",
